From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:45:15 +0930
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] guess-rev.sh: honour OPENOCD_LOCAL_VERSION

The local version suffix (e.g. "-01701-gb04ccfef") is derived from the
revision metadata of the tree being built. A distributor that applies
its own patches on top of an upstream commit gets a suffix naming its
own patched commit, which is neither the upstream commit nor the
package version, so a bug report cannot be traced to either.

If OPENOCD_LOCAL_VERSION is set in the environment, print it verbatim
in place of the derived suffix. Unset, nothing changes.
---
 guess-rev.sh | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/guess-rev.sh b/guess-rev.sh
index efe2659..6d6970c 100755
--- a/guess-rev.sh
+++ b/guess-rev.sh
@@ -14,6 +14,13 @@ usage() {
 
 cd "${1:-.}" || usage
 
+# A distributor building from an exported tree knows the version better than
+# the metadata of that tree does: honour it instead of deriving one.
+if [ -n "$OPENOCD_LOCAL_VERSION" ]; then
+	printf '%s' "$OPENOCD_LOCAL_VERSION"
+	exit 0
+fi
+
 # Check for git and a git repo.
 if head=`git rev-parse --verify --short HEAD 2>/dev/null`; then
 
